WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
It was supposed to be easy money.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:10.598
In early 2026, millions of everyday people across China—teachers, cab drivers, students—watched their trading apps light up green on the morning commute.

3
00:00:10.598 --> 00:00:12.136
The rally felt unstoppable.

4
00:00:12.136 --> 00:00:17.150
But behind the hype lay a quiet time bomb: almost everyone was buying on borrowed money.

5
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.075
Then, the market blinked.

6
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:20.955
Just an ordinary two-percent dip.

7
00:00:20.955 --> 00:00:26.140
But when you trade with triple leverage, a tiny tremor isn't a dip—it's an execution order.

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:32.750
Before traders could even unlock their screens, brokerage algorithms took control, dumping collateral into freefall.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.795
On Wall Street, big banks absorb the shock.

10
00:00:35.795 --> 00:00:38.576
But ninety percent of China's market is retail.

11
00:00:38.576 --> 00:00:41.358
It's a crowded theater with only one exit door.

12
00:00:41.358 --> 00:00:47.099
When automated margin calls hit thirty million phones at the exact same second, panic went viral.

13
00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:49.525
Everyone smashed sell—into an empty room.

14
00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:52.806
Beijing threw hundreds of billions into the fire.

15
00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:54.565
State funds bought index funds.

16
00:00:54.565 --> 00:00:56.381
Regulators banned short selling.

17
00:00:56.381 --> 00:01:00.752
But when a bubble built on borrowed faith bursts, you can't print confidence.

18
00:01:00.752 --> 00:01:04.100
Two trillion dollars didn't just vanish—the illusion broke.
